\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath, amssymb}

\title{Module: O1}
\author{SAT\_O Audit Environment}
\date{}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

\section*{Abstract}
This document provides the full theory content and tailored audit instructions for Module O1, corresponding to the ``SAT20 FIRST LOOK: Ultra-Hostile'' report. Auditors are required to validate the module according to the SAT\_O Testing Protocol under Ultra-Hostile conditions.

\section*{Scope}
Module under test: \textbf{SAT20: Ultra-Hostile}

\section*{Methods (Testing Instructions)}
Auditors must adhere strictly to the following instructions:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Definition Consistency}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Identify and list all technical terms.
        \item Verify that each term has a precise and rigorous definition.
        \item Flag any undefined or ambiguously defined terms.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Logical Structure Validation}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Check for internal logical consistency.
        \item Identify unproven assertions, missing derivations, or logical gaps.
        \item Explicitly outline each logical dependency chain.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Mathematical Correctness}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Re-derive all equations step-by-step.
        \item Perform dimensional analysis for each action.
        \item Confirm tensorial and spinorial correctness.
        \item Check topological quantization conditions (e.g., magnetic monopole quantization).
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Group-Theoretical Integrity}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Re-derive SU(2) structure constants and commutation relations.
        \item Verify anomaly cancellation for spinor doublets.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Quantum Consistency Check}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Analyze the emergence of physical constants under quantum corrections.
        \item Propose a plausible renormalization group flow for $\hbar$, $e$, and $G$.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Falsifiability Assessment}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Identify all stated predictions.
        \item Determine which predictions are falsifiable with current or near-future technology.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Independence Verification}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Confirm that no external assumptions are required.
        \item Highlight any dependencies outside the presented theory.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Hidden Parameter Scan}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item List all free parameters.
        \item Verify that all parameters are either derived or physically motivated.
        \item Identify any signs of fine-tuning.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Failure Mode Analysis}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Hypothesize at least one specific failure scenario.
        \item Provide a worked example showing how a prediction could be falsified.
    \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}

\section*{Critical Commentary}
Upon completion, auditors must submit:
\begin{itemize}
    \item A detailed LaTeX audit report (Abstract, Scope, Methods, Findings, Critical Commentary).
    \item No Pass/Fail statements without explicit derivations.
\end{itemize}

\end{document}


