\section*{Tailored Ultra-Hostile Testing Instructions}

The auditor must conduct a full, explicit audit of this module, strictly adhering to the SAT\_O Ultra-Hostile Testing Protocol v3.0:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Definition Consistency:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Identify all specialized terms (e.g., manifold properties, connections, gauge fields).
      \item Verify rigorous definitions are present and unambiguous.
      \item Report any undefined or vague terms.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Logical Structure Validation:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Trace all logical argument flows.
      \item Identify missing proofs, logical leaps, or circular reasoning.
      \item Explicitly document the chain of reasoning.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Mathematical Correctness:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Re-derive all key equations (actions, quantization conditions, field strengths).
      \item Conduct dimensional and unit consistency checks for every critical formula.
      \item Verify tensor index contractions, symmetries, and spinor representations.
      \item Confirm topological quantization conditions (e.g., magnetic monopole quantization) with rigorous derivations.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Group-Theoretical Integrity:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Re-derive SU(2) Lie algebra structure constants and commutation relations.
      \item Confirm the spinor matter content is anomaly-free (specifically Witten anomaly cancellation).
      \item Verify representation theory correctness for gauge fields and matter.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Quantum Consistency Check:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Analyze the emergence of physical constants (\(\hbar\), \(e\), \(G\)) via quantum/topological mechanisms.
      \item Discuss plausible renormalization group (RG) flow behavior for these constants.
      \item Check for loop corrections and their plausible impact on the effective action.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Falsifiability Assessment:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Enumerate all concrete, testable predictions (e.g., magnetic monopole flux quantization, instanton effects).
      \item Discuss if these predictions are currently or prospectively experimentally accessible.
      \item Highlight any unfalsifiable or purely theoretical claims.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Independence Verification:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Confirm the module is self-contained.
      \item Identify any reliance on external inputs or assumptions beyond the given document and glossary.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Hidden Parameter Scan:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Identify all free parameters (e.g., coupling constants, vacuum expectation values).
      \item Verify each parameter is either derived internally or physically motivated.
      \item Detect any indications of fine-tuning or unexplained parameter choices.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Failure Mode Analysis:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Propose at least one plausible physical or mathematical failure mode for the module.
      \item Provide a detailed worked example demonstrating how falsification might occur.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Additional Nontrivial Tests:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item Conduct at least one unexpected or challenging test beyond the baseline checklist.
      \item Examples: boundary condition stability, limit behavior under extreme parameters, emergent constant scaling analysis.
    \end{itemize}

  \item \textbf{Audit Constraints:}
    \begin{itemize}
      \item \textbf{No summary judgments or pass/fail declarations are permitted without explicit derivation.}
      \item \textbf{No theory modifications, fixes, or improvements are allowed.}
      \item \textbf{Every claim must be fully substantiated with step-by-step work.}
    \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}

\end{document}

